subproblem.statement:
Let n ∈ ℕ, let F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ be C¹ and let V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} be open. Then there are open sets Ω_k ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} and maps Θ_k : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^{n+1} (k ∈ ℕ) such that, for every k, all of the following hold:
- Θ_k is C¹ on Ω_k and injective on Ω_k;
- DΘ_k(z) is injective for every z ∈ Ω_k;
- Θ_k(Ω_k) is open and contained in V;
- F(Θ_k(z)) = z_0 for every z ∈ Ω_k.
Moreover every y ∈ V with DF(y) ≠ 0 lies in ⋃_k Θ_k(Ω_k).

Let P, n ∈ ℕ and let c : ℝ → ℝⁿ → ℝ^{n+1} satisfy c(s,w)_0 = s and c(s,w)_{i+1} = w_i. Assume:
- ψ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P is C¹, V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1}, ψ is injective on V and Dψ(y) is injective for y ∈ V;
- F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ is C¹;
- Ω ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} is open, and Θ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^{n+1} is C¹ on Ω and injective on Ω, with DΘ(z) injective for z ∈ Ω, Θ(Ω) ⊆ V and F(Θ(z)) = z_0 for z ∈ Ω.
Fix t ∈ ℝ, and let Ω^t := {w ∈ ℝⁿ : c(t,w) ∈ Ω} and χ(w) := ψ(Θ(c(t,w))). Then Ω^t is open and χ is C¹ and injective on Ω^t. Moreover, for every w ∈ Ω^t, with z := c(t,w) and y := Θ(z):
- DF(y) ≠ 0 and Dχ(w) is injective;
- for every v ∈ Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) with ⟨v, Dψ(y)e⟩ = DF(y)e for all e, Dχ(w)(ℝⁿ) = Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) ∩ (ℝv)^⊥ and √det(Dχ(w)*Dχ(w)) = |v|·√det(Dψ(y)*Dψ(y))·|det DΘ(z)|.

Let P, n ∈ ℕ and write Hᵏ = μHE[k]. Assume:
- ψ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P is C¹, V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} is open, ψ is injective on V and Dψ(y) is injective for y ∈ V;
- F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ is C¹;
- Ω ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} is open, and Θ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^{n+1} is C¹ on Ω and injective on Ω, with DΘ(z) injective for z ∈ Ω, Θ(Ω) ⊆ V and F(Θ(z)) = z_0 for z ∈ Ω;
- Y' ⊆ Θ(Ω) is Borel;
- G : ℝ^P → ℝ^P satisfies G(ψ(y)) ∈ Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) and ⟨G(ψ(y)), Dψ(y)e⟩ = DF(y)e for all y ∈ Y' and e ∈ ℝ^{n+1}.
Then for every Borel g : ℝ^P → [0,∞], the function t ↦ ∫_{ψ(Y'∩F⁻¹(t))} g dHⁿ is Borel and ∫_ℝ ∫_{ψ(Y'∩F⁻¹(t))} g dHⁿ dt = ∫_{ψ(Y')} |G| g dH^{n+1}.

Let P, n ∈ ℕ and t ∈ ℝ, and write Hⁿ = μHE[n]. Assume ψ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P is C¹, V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} is open, ψ is injective on V, Dψ(y) is injective for y ∈ V, and F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ is C¹. Then there are open sets U_j ⊆ ℝⁿ, points a_j ∈ ℝⁿ, radii r_j ∈ ℝ and maps χ_j : ℝⁿ → ℝ^P (j ∈ ℕ) such that for every j:
- closedBall(a_j, r_j) ⊆ U_j;
- χ_j is C¹ on U_j and injective on U_j;
- χ_j(U_j) is countably n-rectifiable, and Hⁿ(χ_j(closedBall(a_j, r_j))) < ∞;
- for every w ∈ U_j, Dχ_j(w) is injective, and there is y ∈ V with ψ(y) = χ_j(w), F(y) = t and DF(y) ≠ 0 such that Dχ_j(w)(ℝⁿ) = Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) ∩ (ℝv)^⊥ for every v ∈ Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) with ⟨v, Dψ(y)e⟩ = DF(y)e for all e.
Moreover ψ({y ∈ V : F(y) = t, DF(y) ≠ 0}) ⊆ ⋃_j χ_j(ball(a_j, r_j)).

Let P, n ∈ ℕ and write Hᵏ = μHE[k]. Assume:
- ψ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P is C¹, V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} is open, ψ is injective on V and Dψ(y) is injective for y ∈ V;
- F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ is C¹;
- Y' ⊆ V is Borel with DF(y) ≠ 0 for all y ∈ Y';
- G : ℝ^P → ℝ^P satisfies G(ψ(y)) ∈ Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) and ⟨G(ψ(y)), Dψ(y)e⟩ = DF(y)e for y ∈ Y' and e ∈ ℝ^{n+1}.
Then for every Borel g : ℝ^P → [0,∞], the function t ↦ ∫_{ψ(Y'∩F⁻¹(t))} g dHⁿ is Borel and ∫_ℝ ∫_{ψ(Y'∩F⁻¹(t))} g dHⁿ dt = ∫_{ψ(Y')} |G| g dH^{n+1}.
